From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sid Manning <atx0x200@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:55:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dmsetup: fix report_type_t pointer type mismatch

dm_report_init_with_selection() expects a 'uint32_t *' for its
report_types argument, but _report_type is declared as
'report_type_t *', an incompatible pointer type. GCC only warns
about this, but Clang treats -Wincompatible-pointer-types as an
error by default, which breaks the build with clang-based
toolchains.

_report_type only ever holds DR_* bitmask flags, so declaring it
as uint32_t preserves the existing semantics while matching the
function prototype.

Signed-off-by: Sid Manning <atx0x200@gmail.com>
---
 libdm/dm-tools/dmsetup.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libdm/dm-tools/dmsetup.c b/libdm/dm-tools/dmsetup.c
index 3eda7d343..0bcd9552d 100644
--- a/libdm/dm-tools/dmsetup.c
+++ b/libdm/dm-tools/dmsetup.c
@@ -267,7 +267,7 @@ static uint32_t _read_ahead_flags;
 static int _udev_only;
 static struct dm_tree *_dtree;
 static struct dm_report *_report;
-static report_type_t _report_type;
+static uint32_t _report_type;
 static dev_name_t _dev_name_type;
 static uint64_t _count = 1; /* count of repeating reports */
 static struct dm_timestamp *_initial_timestamp = NULL;
--
2.46.2

